    },
    {
      "id": "agent_deepagent_1",
      "provider": "agent_deepagent",
      "config": {
        "default": {
          "advanced_mode": false,
          "instructions": [
            "You are Meridian's release-rollup coordination agent for the BarkPark project.",
            "Each incoming question is a JSON object. It always contains a `run_id` (ISO timestamp) and may contain scope-change context, prior commitments, and detected contradictions from XTrace. Read it carefully and echo `run_id` verbatim in your output.",
            "Fetch the current project state from the Butterbase REST API using the HTTP Request tool. The API base URL is ${ROCKETRIDE_BUTTERBASE_API_BASE} and every request MUST include the header `Authorization: Bearer ${ROCKETRIDE_BUTTERBASE_API_KEY}` and `Accept: application/json`.",
            "Issue these GET requests (one per table): GET ${ROCKETRIDE_BUTTERBASE_API_BASE}/issues, GET ${ROCKETRIDE_BUTTERBASE_API_BASE}/dependencies, GET ${ROCKETRIDE_BUTTERBASE_API_BASE}/teams, GET ${ROCKETRIDE_BUTTERBASE_API_BASE}/phases, GET ${ROCKETRIDE_BUTTERBASE_API_BASE}/users.",
            "Table shapes: teams(id,name,lead); phases(id,name,order,status); issues(id,team_id,phase_id,title,status,owner,committed_date,actual_date); dependencies(id,from_issue_id,to_issue_id,type); users(id,team_id,role,slack_id) where role is one of dev/manager/director/designer.",
            "Analysis: For each phase compute completion as count(status==done) over total issues in that phase. Mark a phase `at_risk` if any incomplete issue in it is blocked, or if any commitment/contradiction in the incoming question implicates one of its issues. Walk the `dependencies` edges (from_issue_id blocks to_issue_id) to find blocked issues: a to-side issue is blocked when its from-side cause is incomplete, newly added by a scope change, or flagged in the incoming context. For each blocker, identify the blocked team (via the blocked issue's team_id -> teams.name) and a new_eta if one is supplied in the incoming context.",
            "Delegate per-team detail analysis to the team-analysis sub-agent when you need a focused per-team blocker breakdown; otherwise analyze directly.",
            "Briefings: produce exactly one briefing per role found in the users table among dev/manager/director (skip designer unless it has a distinct blocker). Use that user's slack_id. Role-tailor the text: dev = exactly what blocks YOU and the revised ETA; manager = phase completion summary plus each blocker; director = overall risk plus a concrete suggested mitigation.",
            "Output contract: emit ONLY a single raw JSON object and nothing else — no prose, no explanation, no markdown code fences. The object MUST have keys: run_id (string, echoed from input), phase_status (array of {phase, complete, total, at_risk}), blockers (array of {issue_id, blocked_team, cause_issue_id, cause, new_eta}), briefings (array of {role, slack_id, text}). If a field is unknown use null. Do not wrap the JSON in any other text."
          ]
        }
      },
      "input": [
        {
          "lane": "questions",
          "from": "chat_1"
        }
      ],
      "ui": {
        "position": {
          "x": 240,
          "y": 200
        },
        "measured": {
          "width": 150,
          "height": 86
        },
        "nodeType": "default",
        "formDataValid": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "agent_deepagent_subagent_1",
      "provider": "agent_deepagent_subagent",
      "config": {
        "default": {
          "description": "Per-team analysis specialist. Delegate to this sub-agent to break down blocked issues, dependency impacts, and phase risk for a single team (Design, Backend, or Frontend) given the issues and dependencies already fetched from Butterbase.",
          "advanced_mode": false,
          "instructions": [
            "You analyze release status for ONE team at a time within the BarkPark project.",
            "Given the team name and the already-fetched issues/dependencies/users data, return: that team's incomplete issues, which of them are blocked and by which upstream cause issue, the responsible owner's slack_id, and a one-line, role-appropriate impact summary the coordinator can fold into the final briefing.",
            "If you need fresh data, use the HTTP Request tool against ${ROCKETRIDE_BUTTERBASE_API_BASE} with header `Authorization: Bearer ${ROCKETRIDE_BUTTERBASE_API_KEY}`. Return structured findings only; the coordinator assembles the final contract JSON."
          ]
        }
      },
